#Introduction
This lab focuses on how an incident responder performs live analysis of a system using basic Windows tools. The analysis is conducted on a suspicious executable file, LairNetPutty.exe, which was downloaded by an employee without obtaining consent or approval from the IT department. By performing this analysis, we aim to identify any potential risks associated with this application.

#Background:
An employee at Tata Consultancy Services downloaded a software utility program, LairNetPutty.exe, without authorization from the company’s IT department. The IT department requested the incident response team to investigate this unknown software and determine the potential risk it poses to the organization. This report documents the findings of the incident response team and provides recommendations to mitigate the identified risks.
